 "instructions": "Translate every \"en\" string into Simplified Chinese (zh-Hans), game-guide register. Follow glossary.json strictly. Keep ⟦0⟧-style placeholders, numbers, units and wiki markup exactly. Return only {\"items\":[{\"k\":\"...\",\"zh\":\"...\"}]} with the same k values.",
 "units": [
  {
   "k": "13ho76s",
   "en": "As Communist China, fight both China and Japan before 1940 within 90 days of being at war with the other, and capitulate them both."
  },
  {
   "k": "1h0k7yc",
   "en": "Strategy"
  },
  {
   "k": "1e1piyf",
   "en": "⟦0⟧: The requirements are a little vague & may actually be buggy. To be safe, put at least a one day gap between your war declarations on China and Japan. That should avoid any bugs that (still) may exist.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "5mau71",
   "en": "Note"
  },
  {
   "k": "ic7jdq",
   "en": "You need to declare war on China and Japan before 1940. Capitulation on the other hand has no time limit. The requirement to \"capitulated\" means you must achieve the highest score in the war against China and the highest score in the war against Japan."
  },
  {
   "k": "bb20xd",
   "en": "The easiest way and probably also the most consistent way is to turn off Historical and restart until Japan goes down their Democratic / Communist path (left side of the political focus tree). This way Japan does not attack China and gives you nearly 4 years to prepare your wars with both countries. Put China on Historical. The event in which Japan's political future gets decided fires after 50 days, so resetting doesn't waste a lot of time."
  },
  {
   "k": "1wf3gk0",
   "en": "During those prep years, focus first on getting a bit on an economy. Go down the middle path of the focus tree until at least ⟦0⟧. Taking ⟦1⟧ and ⟦2⟧ is not required, but the buffs are nice. After that go down the right side of the focus tree, pick ⟦3⟧ and continue until ⟦4⟧ Have one factory on artillery and the rest on guns. Later on add trains, Anti-Air and Trucks (but only when you can produce a good amount of guns and arty on a steady base).",
   "frags": 5
  },
  {
   "k": "1sxxav9",
   "en": "Specialize CSCEC - Military Industry"
  },
  {
   "k": "1nj2v20",
   "en": "Allow Trade of Special Goods"
  },
  {
   "k": "loer8s",
   "en": "Promote Paper Bank Notes"
  },
  {
   "k": "xo6y46",
   "en": "Instill Three Rules of Discipline"
  },
  {
   "k": "900jjo",
   "en": "Cooperate with Ulanhu"
  },
  {
   "k": "5i5yhc",
   "en": "For your army, focus on Militias and put your first 100 pp in Zhu De for Army xp. Keep mass assault as you doctrine and for sub-doctrines pick: \"Guerilla Warfare\", \"People's Militia\" and a bit later on \"Artillery & Combat Support\". Over time increase your militia template (Renmin Jundui) to 20 with and add support arty. Later on, if you can, add support Anti-Air and one artillery battalion (which results in 22.2 combat with)"
  },
  {
   "k": "1nid6z5",
   "en": "After ⟦0⟧, go to the left side of the focus tree and take the ⟦1⟧ and ⟦2⟧. At this point your army is already strong enough to easily win both border wars. Continue with ⟦3⟧ and ⟦4⟧ With the factories you got form the border wars you should (if not already done) be able to increase yours militias to 20 with. Which is sufficient to destroy and annex Shanxi, The Northeastern Army, Gansu Ma and Ningxia Ma. In the mean time go down the infiltration route and after that work towards ⟦5⟧. If you're lucky you get Shandong.",
   "frags": 6
  },
  {
   "k": "vp3w0k",
   "en": "The Westward Expansion"
  },
  {
   "k": "1a7c45u",
   "en": "The Eastward Expedition"
  },
  {
   "k": "1tmhpkj",
   "en": "The Unwilling Diarchy"
  },
  {
   "k": "6uviym",
   "en": "Bring War to Neighboring Warlords"
  },
  {
   "k": "n7fibb",
   "en": "Demand the Loyalty of the Warlords"
  },
  {
   "k": "lpslqq",
   "en": "Make sure your War Goals are ready by November 1939 by taking ⟦0⟧ and ⟦1⟧ in time. 36 – 48 Militia Units with Support and one Line Arty should be sufficient to hold off and China. Together with how much you were able to infiltrate taking out China should be easy. With Historical AI off there is a good chance China joins a faction , ensuring you get the capitulation before any possible peace deal. With China's industry added to yours, protecting your coastline against Japanese naval invasions is easy. Just create a 12-with militia template with Artillery Support and spam enough of them.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "xokd89",
   "en": "Expel the Occupiers"
  },
  {
   "k": "14ve2aw",
   "en": "Preemptive Strike"
  },
  {
   "k": "1502skh",
   "en": "Now only Japan is left. Start researching paratroopers and transport planes and in the meantime focus on taking out the Warlords in the north / north-east and conquer Korea after that. Now all you have to do is build an airfield in \"Gyeongsang\" and from there paradrop on to the Japanese mainland. You don't need an Airforce for this, Japan often doesn't put theirs in the sky or you simply have to wait a little bit (Or simply reload the safe, it takes a few in game ours before air-superiority is registered). Your paratroopers will go (eventually). The Japanese AI doesn't properly protect the Home Isles with soldiers either, simply have your army waiting In a / multiple ports. Once your paratroopers take one simply transport them over (don't worry about them getting intercepted, the Navy AI seems to be passive in patch 1.17) and capitulate Japan. Same as China, Japan may have joined / created a faction which basically ensures you'll see an capitulation before any possible peace deal."
  },
